<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">W. C. Handy and his Memphis Blues Band</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1922</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Bessie Smith with Louis Armstrong</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1925</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">St. Louis Blues (film, Bessie Smith)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1929</span><span class="sg-chain-h">film built on the song</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Louis Armstrong &amp; His Orchestra, with Red Allen</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1929</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Rhapsody in Blue (George Gershwin)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Handy's themes borrowed</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Baby Face and Banjo on My Knee (films; sung by Theresa Harris)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Tav Falco's Panther Burns, Behind the Magnolia Curtain</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1981</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Herbie Hancock with Stevie Wonder, Gershwin's World</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1998</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li></ul></section>
